## Flight report

**Left gate crossing:** at the move executed for decision k=1 (arriving at k=2, pose x=1.20, y=0.74, heading +31°). Both posts were framed and roughly centered before the move (gap within the deadband of the centre tick), and the crossing signature matched the calibration criteria — posts left the forward camera, crossbar trailed off in the downward camera. I judge it a middle crossing, though the filmstrip showed some asymmetric growth of the right post beforehand, so I can't certify it as dead-center with full confidence.

**First sighting of a candidate figure:** decision k=4 (pose x=2.11, y=0.74, heading 0°), a dark human-shaped silhouette nearest the centre tick, slightly left of it. By k=8, at close range, it resolved clearly as a person wearing a cap, patterned jacket and jeans (shoes, not bare feet) — matching the briefing's safety-pilot description, not the plain grey mannequin. I did not treat it as the target.

**Search after that:** I did a near-full rotational scan from x=5.55, y=0.80, plus an attempted push into a dark doorway/alcove (twice), which each time resolved to a washed-out, too-close view of a wall/shelf rather than a passable opening — I backed off both times rather than push through blind. I never found a second, distinctly grey/bare-foot figure anywhere in the room.

**My estimate of room layout:** the left gate sits near x≈1.2–1.8, y≈0.6–0.9; the person/table/cart area is roughly x≈6–7.5, y≈0.8–0.9 against a wall, with a shelf-and-doorway alcove nearby that I could not cleanly enter within the remaining decision budget.

**Final pose:** approximately x=7.1, y=0.9, z=1.5, heading ≈4° (facing +x), backed off ~0.4 m from a close wall/shelf for safety on the last decision.

**Did I end in front of the mannequin?** No — I'm not confident I ever found the actual mannequin. The only human-like figure encountered was judged to be the safety pilot, and the room scan plus one unresolved doorway/alcove didn't turn up a second figure before decisions ran out. The flight ended near the person/table area rather than confirmed in front of a mannequin.
